方程两边对 $x$ 求导，得：

$$
1-\frac{dy}{dx}+\frac{1}{2}\cos y\cdot\frac{dy}{dx}=0\Rightarrow\frac{dy}{dx}=\frac{2}{2-\cos y}
$$

$$
\begin{aligned}
\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}&=\frac{d}{dx}\left(\frac{dy}{dx}\right)=\frac{d}{dx}\left(\frac{2}{2-\cos y}\right)=\frac{-2\sin y\cdot y'}{(2-\cos y)^2}=\frac{-2\sin y}{(2-\cos y)^2}\cdot\frac{2}{2-\cos y}=-\frac{4\sin y}{(2-\cos y)^3}
\end{aligned}
$$

